;; expect: main.e_only refused absurd_needs_init
;; a refuted row is Init's absurd applied to a proof and its negation — an L term, read on the typed
;; route and erased to the refuted row. A body read E-first (here: its result is a Symbol, which has
;; no L reading) cannot write one: the pointer names the route, as dif's does.
(fn e_only ((n Nat)) Symbol (if (= n 0) (quote z) (absurd 1 2)))
